      "Language": "dut",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 23-year-old man had a painful right hand after punching a wall. The base of the second metacarpal was swollen and painful. The base of the second metacarpal is difficult to assess radiologically, due to overlying structures. After a trauma, additional slight oblique X-rays may help to make a diagnosis."},
